          "title": "unrepresentable n-partition gate is implemented but not a public decider"
        },
        {
          "detail": "docs/plan/102-exact-clearance-candidate.md calls the rapidly-alternating 200-span representation a safe curve with a dense maximum of 57.6 m/s (ratio 2.08) versus V = 120 m/s. The on-disk alternating_witness() that produces V = 120, 200 spans and 60200 evaluations is unsafe (true net ~0.20 m). The quadratic B-spline of alternating +/-120 derivative controls has mid-span value 0.125*120 + 0.75*(-120) + 0.125*120 = -60, so the true supremum is 60.0 m/s and the true ratio is 2.00. 57.6 appears only on the 1001-point grid u = 0, 0.001, ..., 1.0, whose step is one tenth of the 0.01 s control-alternation period and never hits a span midpoint. Conservative direction: it over-states how loose V is. No certificate field changes.",
